      "date": "2026-10-10 12:28:33.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(3 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nThe fix itself looks correct: the lpn_peer ownership check closes the cross-peer list_move() in lnet_peer_merge_data(), and the list moves are now done under LNET_LOCK_EX like lnet_peer_attach_peer_ni(). A couple of commit-message points and one question about the user-visible effect of the new -EALREADY are inline; none of them needs a re-spin on its own. Since this fixes an LBUG, is a sanity-lnet reproducer feasible? For example: a Lustre-locked multi-NID peer whose primary NID is then advertised by a different peer record during discovery. That would protect the lpn_peer check from future regressions.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    }
