        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Serguei Smirnov",
          "email": "ssmirnov@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-08 21:04:02.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "subject": "LU-20515 lnet: prevent peer net list corruption during discovery",
        "message": "LU-20515 lnet: prevent peer net list corruption during discovery\n\nWhen a discovered NID belongs to another peer with a locked\nprimary NID, lnet_peer_add_nid() rejects the addition but\nincorrectly returns success.\n\nDuring discovery merging, lnet_peer_merge_data() may then move\nthe advertised primary NID's peer net onto the current peer's\nlist without updating its ownership or reference count. This\ncan leave the peer lists inconsistent and trigger an assertion\nin lnet_destroy_peer_locked() when the peer is released.\n\nReturn -EALREADY when the locked-primary conflict is detected,\npreserving the existing peer configuration without triggering\nthe forced merge behavior associated with -EEXIST.\n\nOnly reorder the primary peer net and peer NI when they belong\nto the peer being updated. Protect the list operations with\nthe exclusive LNet network lock to synchronize with readers.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lnet\nSigned-off-by: Serguei Smirnov <ssmirnov@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I90e05241a1bfee6dcb3842774a43a0dc4a3a4748\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
